course: dictionary
lesson: 12228
title: Conserve: save and protect
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To conserve something means to use it carefully so it is not wasted, or to look after it so it lasts. «We must conserve water during the dry summer.» Water is precious, so we use less of it. Conserve means save.
explain: The words around conserve give you clues about what is being saved or protected. «The park rangers work to conserve the wildlife in the forest.» Rangers look after animals and plants, so conserve here means protect.
explain: The verb changes its ending: conserve, conserves, conserved, conserving. «She conserved her energy by walking slowly up the hill.» She saved her strength for later. Ask yourself: what is being saved, or what is being protected?
fact: Conserve is a verb, so it is something you do.
fact: «Conserve» means to save something so it is not wasted or used up, such as water, energy or money.
fact: «Conserve» also means to protect nature or old buildings so they stay in good condition.
fact: «Conservation» is the noun for protecting nature.
fact: In physics, energy is «conserved»: it is never made or destroyed, only changed from one form to another.
exercise: «Please conserve water by turning off the tap.» What does conserve mean here? | Make it hotter | Spill it all over the floor | *Save it so it is not wasted | Sell it to a shop
exercise: «The charity works hard to conserve old buildings in the town.» What does conserve mean here? | To count them | *To protect them so they stay in good condition | To paint them bright red | To knock them down
exercise: Ella asks, «What is the noun for protecting nature?» | *Conservation | Conserving | Conserve | Conserved
test: «Mum said, "Let's conserve energy and switch off the lights."» What does conserve energy mean? | Use it up quickly | Turn it into a song | *Use it carefully so it is not wasted | Share it with the neighbours
test: In a long race, runners conserve their energy at the start. Why do they do this? | To eat their lunch early | *To save strength for the end of the race | To run out of breath quickly | To stop and sit down
exam: Which meaning fits in «The volunteers conserve the old church for future visitors»? | To paint it | To count it | To waste it | *To protect it
